<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29855" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἒ ἔ</span></b> , or repeated <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἒ ἒ ἒ ἔ</span></b> , an exclamation of pain or
		grief; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>woe! woe</i>! <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1114
			</span></i>, etc.; always doubled either once or twice and better
			written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐέ</span> (as in cod. 
				Med.
			 of <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>), or (where the metre requires an iambus) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					149
				</span></i>
			; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠέ</span> cod. 
				Med.
			 in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				966
			</span></i>.</div>
